  "description": "The short way up Ukraine's highest peak. A marked footpath leaves the Zaroslyak trailhead at about 1,290 m and climbs 740 m in 3.8 km — roughly a 20% average gradient — over Mala Hoverla (1,762 m) to the 2,061 m summit. OpenStreetMap rates the path as plain hiking (SAC T1), with no technical sections, but the steepness makes it a real mountain day: allow two to three hours up. Two springs and two camp spots are mapped within 150 m of the track.\n\nRoute data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). OSM relation/10330801.\nCover photo: Khoroshkov / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wikimedia Commons.",
